  },
  "body": "Buffer contiguous character insertions in the HTML parser's `pending text` tuple `(insertion location, data)` and flush via DOM's *replace data* when appending to an existing preceding `Text` node (running the parent's *children changed steps* and queueing a `\"characterData\"` `MutationRecord`).\n\nThis reflects current interoperable reality.\n\n`pending text` is flushed:\n- in the *tree construction dispatcher* when a non-character token is emitted from the tokenizer;\n- at the end of the networking task queue tasks that process input byte chunks when loading HTML and plain-text documents;\n- at the start of *insert a foreign element* (e.g., when a non-whitespace character token triggers implicit `<body>` creation or active formatting element reconstruction);\n- in *insert a character* when the adjusted insertion location changes;\n- in *\"in table text\"*'s *\"Anything else\"* branch before switching back to the original insertion mode and reprocessing the token;\n- in *abort a parser*;\n- at the end of *run a fragment parser*; and\n- at the end of the *document write steps*.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64800.\n\nFixes #12744.\n\n---\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (already implements matching behavior)\n   * Gecko (already implements matching behavior)\n   * WebKit (already implements matching behavior)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64800\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: already matches for document parsing; streaming HTML edge cases tracked in https://issues.chromium.org/issues/581018331. Slight mismatch in https://issues.chromium.org/issues/581920330.\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2089766 for slight mismatch; streaming HTML tracked in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2043150\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=330912\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13199/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 12:31 PM UTC (5f89cb7)\">/document-lifecycle.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13199/289f918...5f89cb7/document-lifecycle.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 12:31 PM UTC (5f89cb7)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13199/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 12:31 PM UTC (5f89cb7)\">/dynamic-markup-insertion.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13199/289f918...5f89cb7/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 12:31 PM UTC (5f89cb7)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13199/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 12:31 PM UTC (5f89cb7)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13199/289f918...5f89cb7/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 12:31 PM UTC (5f89cb7)\">diff</a> )",
